            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of acute abdominal pain in a child: an inverted Meckel diverticulum: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>314-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jcu.20681</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inverted Meckel diverticulum has been reported as a lead point for intussusception in children. However all cases of isolated inversion of a Meckel diverticulum have involved adults in whom the diagnosis was clinically unexpected. We describe the sonographic appearance of isolated inversion of Meckel diverticulum in a 3-year-old boy with acute abdominal symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
